DESCRIPTION:Tragedy struck the circus many times. The trapeze artist's palm
 s became inexplicably sweaty and slick\, utterly unmanageable. He lost his 
 nerve and his partner fell in love with a particularly daring accountant. T
 he lion tamer\, famous throughout the world\, became\, shall we say\, a lit
 tle too interested in the inner workings of his beasts. The jugglers\, two 
 brothers who's proficiency had amazed audiences in Russia\, China\, North K
 orea... incurably quarreled- "you throw too fast\, you always sleep on my s
 ide of the bed\, everyone likes you better" until one left to pursue his li
 felong interest in microbiology\, the other the bottle... The freaks all to
 ok their money for plastic surgery in Thailand... And the clowns were a hop
 eless bunch who ended up in politics. But the band stubbornly played on and
  on\, until the last of the popcorn and elephant poop had all been swept aw
 ay\, and the lights turned down... all who had stayed awake agreed\, it had
  been a good night at the circus...\n\nCome see Berlin's favorite anarchicb
 alkanjazzswing orchestra and dance the night away!\n\nEntry: 5€ in vintage 
 costume\, 7€ without (a pair of suspenders\, people\, a pair of suspenders 
 is all you need. A bowtie would also be ok.)\n\nAt Queen Qotti\, Adalbertst
 r 98.\nDance begins at 22h.\n\n-mh
