DESCRIPTION:Do you like dancing to live music? GREAT! Then you should check
  out our monthly live swing jam session.\n\n\nThe phrase "jam session" came
  about in the 1920s when white and black musicians would congregate after t
 heir regular paying gigs\, to play the jazz they could not play in the band
 s they played in. When Bing Crosby would attend these sessions\, the musici
 ans would say he was "jammin' the beat"\, since he would clap on the one an
 d the three. Thus these sessions became known as "jam sessions".\n\nHow coo
 l would it be to dance to this improvised music! Let's get swing musicians 
 and dancers together once a month in our Monday Marmalade and swing it all 
 the night through!\n\n2€ at the door. If you appreciate the live music\, pl
 ease tip the band ♥\n\n-of-
