DESCRIPTION:On 09.03. we'll have the distinct pleasure of hearing six of Be
 rlin's best musicians (the Musicomaniacs) interpret the hot jazz music of t
 he John Kirby Sextet. The Sextet was one of the great small groups at the e
 nd of the 30s\, six guys in coats and tails playing intricate\, extremely c
 ool arrangements written by trumpet Charlie Shavers and Kirby himself. The 
 songs range from standards like "Blue Skies" and "Undecided" (written by Sh
 avers and first recorded by the Sextet in 1938!)\, to classically-inspired 
 pieces which evoke Haydn\, Tchaikovsky\, and Beethoven\, among others.\n\nO
 f the Sextet's music we find the classically-inspired stuff to be the most 
 fun to just sit and listen to\, but the originals and classic interpretatio
 ns are even better for dancing- the Sextet's 1938 recordings of "From A Fla
 t to C" and "Undecided" are surely known to every Balboa dancer. And the sl
 ower groove of "The Turf" and "It's Only A Paper Moon" will be sure to make
  lindy hoppers happy.\n\nA word to the room: we'll hear all of this lovelin
 ess in one of the most gorgeous venues of Berlin- Tangoloft\, with its beau
 tiful grand piano and spacious parquet floors.\n\nEntry: 20€\n\nDoors 20h\n
 Band starts around 21h.\nDJ'd music before and after the band.\n\nTangoloft
  can be a little tricky to find- go into the Hof-entrance at Gerichtstr 23 
 and head straight back- don't go into the third Hof/courtyard! It's just pa
 st the CrossFit gym on the right. There are signs hanging up to help you fi
 nd it.\n\nBe careful on the stairs! There's a light switch on the right jus
 t as you come into the stairwell\; we're on the first floor.\n\nhttps://www
 .facebook.com/events/377834282629055/\n\n-mh
LAST-MODIFIED:20180309T200010Z
LOCATION:Tangoloft\, Gerichtstraße 23\, 13347 Berlin\, Germany
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Club Kirby
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
