DESCRIPTION:Do you like dancing to live music? GREAT! Then you should check
  out our monthly live swing jam session:\n\nThe phrase "jam session" came a
 bout in the 1920s when white and black musicians would congregate after the
 ir regular paying gigs\, to play the jazz they could not play in the bands 
 they played in. When Bing Crosby would attend these sessions\, the musician
 s would say he was "jammin' the beat"\, since he would clap on the one and 
 the three. Thus these sessions became known as "jam sessions".\n\nHow cool 
 would it be to dance to this improvised music! Let's get swing musicians an
 d dancers together once a month in our Monday Marmalade and swing it all th
 e night through!\n\nNo cover charge\, but if you appreciate the live music\
 , then tip the band ♥\n\nJoin & Share the FB event:\nhttps://www.facebook.c
 om/events/1822884027739529/\n\n-of-
LAST-MODIFIED:20170911T122443Z
LOCATION:Marie-Antoinette\, Holzmarktstraße 15-18 \, Berlin\, Deutschland
SEQUENCE:4
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Monday Marmalade - Live Swing Jam @ Marie-Antoinette (SwingStep)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
