DESCRIPTION:Do you like dancing to live music? GREAT! Then you should check
  out our live swing jam session\, NOW BACK FROM THE SUMMER BREAK: \n\n\nThe
  phrase "jam session" came about in the 1920s when white and black musician
 s would congregate after their regular paying gigs\, to play the jazz they 
 could not play in the bands they played in. When Bing Crosby would attend t
 hese sessions\, the musicians would say he was "jammin' the beat"\, since h
 e would clap on the one and the three. Thus these sessions became known as 
 "jam sessions".\n\nHow cool would it be to dance to this improvised music! 
 Let's get swing musicians and dancers together once a month in our Monday M
 armalade and swing it all the night through!\n\n2€ at the door. If you appr
 eciate the live music\, please tip the band ♥\n\n-of-
LAST-MODIFIED:20181111T180442Z
LOCATION:Marie-Antoinette\, Holzmarktstraße 15-18 \, Berlin\, Deutschland
SEQUENCE:4
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Monday Marmalade: Live Swing Jam @ Marie-Antoinette (SwingStep)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
