DESCRIPTION:Do you like dancing to live music? GREAT! Then you should check
  out our new live swing jam session:\n\nThe phrase "jam session" came about
  in the 1920s when white and black musicians would congregate after their r
 egular paying gigs\, to play the jazz they could not play in the bands they
  played in. When Bing Crosby would attend these sessions\, the musicians wo
 uld say he was "jammin' the beat"\, since he would clap on the one and the 
 three. Thus these sessions became known as "jam sessions".\n\nHow cool woul
 d it be to dance to this improvised music! Let's get swing musicians and da
 ncers together once a month in our Monday Marmalade and swing it all the ni
 ght through!\n\nNo cover charge\, but if you appreciate the live music\, th
 en tip the band ♥\n-of-
LAST-MODIFIED:20180309T115835Z
LOCATION:Marie-Antoinette\, Holzmarktstraße 15-18 \, Berlin\, Deutschland
SEQUENCE:3
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Monday Social @ Marie-Antoinette (SwingStep)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
