DESCRIPTION:The phrase "jam session" came about in the 1920s when white and
  black musicians would congregate after their regular paying gigs\, to play
  the jazz they could not play in the bands they played in. When Bing Crosby
  would attend these sessions\, the musicians would say he was "jammin' the 
 beat"\, since he would clap on the one and the three. Thus these sessions b
 ecame known as "jam sessions".\n\nHow cool would it be to dance to this imp
 rovised music! Let's get swing musicians and dancers together once a month 
 in our Monday Marmalade and swing it all the night through!\n\nNo cover cha
 rge\, but if you appreciate the live music\, then tip the band <3\n\n- of -
LAST-MODIFIED:20170911T122431Z
LOCATION:Rudolfstr. 1-8\, 10245 Berlin (Jeder ist Tanzbar\, vis à vis Einga
 ng Matrix\, Gewerbehof!)
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Monday Marmalade - Live Swing Jam @ SwingStep Berlin
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
