CREATED:20140317T162243Z
DESCRIPTION:<span>Do you like dancing to live music? GREAT! Then you should
  check out our monthly live swing jam session:</span><br><span><br></span><
 br><span>The phrase "jam session" came about in the 1920s when white and bl
 ack musicians would congregate after their regular paying gigs\, to play th
 e jazz they could not play in the bands they played in. When Bing Crosby wo
 uld attend these sessions\, the musicians would say he was "jammin' the bea
 t"\, since he would clap on the one and the three. Thus these sessions beca
 me known as "jam sessions".</span><br><span><br></span><br><span>How cool w
 ould it be to dance to this improvised music! Let's get swing musicians and
  dancers together once a month in our Monday Marmalade and swing it all the
  night through!</span><br><span><br></span><br><span>2€ at the door. If you
  appreciate the live music\, please tip the band some extra ♥&nbsp\;</span>
 <br><span><br></span><br><span>-of-</span>
LAST-MODIFIED:20180320T164957Z
LOCATION:Marie-Antoinette\, Holzmarktstraße 15-18 \, Berlin\, Deutschland
SEQUENCE:4
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Monday Marmalade - Live Swing Jam @ Marie-Antoinette (SwingStep)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
