DESCRIPTION:Live music\, Count Basie\, hot feet\, cool parquet- continuing 
 the tradition of lofty Saturday dances\, we'll dance way up high at Nou Tan
 go. Two rooms\, hot swing on the main floor and more swinging variety in th
 e backroom. If you need a break from moving it on the floor\, kick back in 
 salon seats and enjoy the show- or the night lights of the city!\n\nPlaying
  hot swinging jazz from 22h with Nou's beautiful old piano and other fine j
 azz implements- The Sunday Night Stompers\, led by Harlem stride-player Cam
 ille will play some swinging piano for us\, accompanied by a bass\, clarine
 t\, and drummer. Stride is a style of piano playing made most famous by Fat
 s Waller\, also played by jazz greats James P. Johnson\, Pete Johnson\, and
  Art Tatum. Fine dancing music for swing!\n\nIn the backroom tonight: Bla B
 la Balboa with DJs Okashi Sensei and Don Atilio.\n\nEntry 7-10€\n\nhttps://
 www.facebook.com/events/203108816765416/
LAST-MODIFIED:20161118T133750Z
LOCATION:Nou Tango Berlin\, Chausseestr 102
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Uptown Lodown Live Sunday Night Stompers
TRANSP:OPAQUE
