DESCRIPTION:<span style="white-space: pre-wrap\; background-color: rgb(255\
 , 255\, 255)\;">Do you like dancing to live music? GREAT! Then you should c
 heck out our monthly live swing jam session:The phrase "jam session" came a
 bout in the 1920s when white and black musicians would congregate after the
 ir regular paying gigs\, to play the jazz they could not play in the bands 
 they played in. When Bing Crosby would attend these sessions\, the musician
 s would say he was "jammin' the beat"\, since he would clap on the one and 
 the three. Thus these sessions became known as "jam sessions".How cool woul
 d it be to dance to this improvised music! Let's get swing musicians and da
 ncers together once a month in our Monday Marmalade and swing it all the ni
 ght through!2€ at the door. If you appreciate the live music\, please tip t
 he band some extra ♥ -of-</span>
LAST-MODIFIED:20181111T180442Z
LOCATION:Marie-Antoinette\, Holzmarktstraße 15-18 \, Berlin\, Deutschland
