CREATED:20220809T140547Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><b>Tickets at the door: </b>25EUR</html-blob><br><ht
 ml-blob><br></html-blob><br><html-blob><u></u><b>Welcome to the party!&nbsp
 \;</b>For this first edition\, we have a fantastic line-up of bands and mus
 icians to carry the music all through the night. Each concert will lead to 
 a Jam Session in the style of our regular Jam Cats Session where musicians 
 and dancers can share the stage. Additionally to that we have planned a lot
  of cool activities also during the daytime:<br><br><b>Dancers&nbsp\;</b>– 
 This festival is for you! All the parties focus on dance music and to warm 
 you up we will offer you some fun dance and movement related tasters on Thu
 rsday\, Friday and Sunday – as well as some lectures and panel discussions 
 on Friday and Saturday Afternoon. By the way: Come as you are! Feel free to
  dance solo\, with a partner\, lead\, follow\, switch… Make the music your 
 friend\, bring your own spin to the style\, and don’t be afraid to stand ou
 t. We make no differentiation based on level\, dance style\, or role and we
 lcome all of your happy feet!<br><br><b>Musicians&nbsp\;</b>– We also organ
 ize music workshops during the day where you can practice and learn with pr
 ofessional musicians from the Syncopation Society. These workshops will tak
 e place alongside lectures and panel discussions accessible to all particip
 ants. We will discuss music styles\, history\, and the cultural significanc
 e of jazz today. More fun awaits you with special daytime activities and ta
 sters curated for the occasion. More to be announced soon.<br><br><b>Everyo
 ne&nbsp\;</b>– We want to use this festival as a chance to educate ourselve
 s in cultural topics that are connected to\, but go beyond the dance and mu
 sic community today. Which is why we on Friday and Saturday afternoon we of
 fer a set of lectures and panel discussions around the topics of Black Amer
 ican Culture\, Diversity and Inclusivity. These topics are very important t
 o us\, so we hope you show up and show your support.<br><br><b>Program For 
 Sunday:<br><br>15:15 – Cine-concert – Charlie Chaplin The immigrant</b><br>
 more info soon...<br><br><b>20:30 – Dance Taster with Joren: Your body\, yo
 ur instrument –Swing dancing from an African perspective<br></b>Music is ex
 pressing yourself through your instrument of choise. When your instrument i
 s your voice\, we call it singing. When it’s your body\, we call it dance. 
 Do you know some swing steps and basic counting? Or you don’t know any of t
 hat? Never mind! This time we will fly into swing from an other angle. How 
 do Africans and Black Americans traditionally get to music and dance? How m
 ight the pioneers of Swing have discovered their basics? What happens when 
 rhythm\, groove and conversation become your starting point?&nbsp\;<br><br>
 <b>21:30 – The Big Jam Allstar Band<br></b>A Jam Session is an after-hour w
 here musicians can blow freely and hang without the constraints of their us
 ual engagements. We want to communicate the excitement of an improvised set
  on the dance-floor and bring this vibe to the festival to create a moment 
 on stage for unique musical encounters. Now we don’t call this the ALL-STAR
  JAM BAND for no reason:&nbsp\;<strong>Meschiya Lake</strong>\,&nbsp\;<stro
 ng>Nana Carling</strong>\,&nbsp\;<strong>Ewan Bleach</strong>\,&nbsp\;<stro
 ng>Mauro Porro</strong>\,&nbsp\;<strong>Malte Tönißen</strong>&nbsp\;and&nb
 sp\;<strong>David Hermlin</strong>&nbsp\;are all headliners in their name. 
 They will meet on stage for the first time\, and we will be there to see it
 !&nbsp\;And just like JAM CATS\, the stage will be open for more musicians 
 afterward. It’s going to be a splendid and one-of-a-kind evening.&nbsp\;<br
 ><br><b>More infos here:</b><br><a href="https://syncopation.de/areyou/"><u
 ><u>https://syncopation.de/areyou/</u></u></a><br><u></u><br>-of-<u></u></h
 tml-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220929T132656Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Are You Syncopated?! - All Star Band @ Ballhaus Prinzenallee
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
