DESCRIPTION:Do you like dancing to live music? GREAT! Then you should check
  out our monthly live swing jam session with the finest and bestest jazz mu
 sicians in Berlin. You cannot miss it!\n\nThe phrase "jam session" came abo
 ut in the 1920s when white and black musicians would congregate after their
  regular paying gigs\, to play the jazz they could not play in the bands th
 ey played in. When Bing Crosby would attend these sessions\, the musicians 
 would say he was "jammin' the beat"\, since he would clap on the one and th
 e three. Thus these sessions became known as "jam sessions".\n\nHow cool wo
 uld it be to dance to this improvised music! Let's get swing musicians and 
 dancers together once a month in our Monday Marmalade and swing it all the 
 night through!\n\n𝑇ℎ𝑖𝑠 𝑖𝑠 𝑎 𝑠𝑤𝑖𝑛𝑔 𝑗𝑎𝑚 𝑠𝑒𝑠𝑠𝑖𝑜𝑛 𝑖𝑛𝑡𝑒
 𝑛𝑑𝑒𝑑 𝑓𝑜𝑟 𝑑𝑎𝑛𝑐𝑒𝑟𝑠\, 𝑗𝑎𝑧𝑧 𝑙𝑜𝑣𝑒𝑟𝑠 𝑎𝑛𝑑 𝑚𝑢𝑠𝑖𝑐𝑖
 𝑎𝑛𝑠. 𝐴𝑟𝑒 𝑦𝑜𝑢 𝑐𝑜𝑚𝑖𝑛𝑔 𝑡𝑜 𝑑𝑎𝑛𝑐𝑒 𝑜𝑟 𝑒𝑛𝑗𝑜𝑦 𝑡ℎ𝑒 𝑚
 𝑢𝑠𝑖𝑐? \n𝑊𝑒 𝑎𝑠𝑘 𝑓𝑜𝑟 5-8€ 𝑎𝑡 𝑡ℎ𝑒 𝑑𝑜𝑜𝑟. 𝐴𝑟𝑒 𝑦𝑜𝑢 𝑐𝑜
 𝑚𝑖𝑛𝑔 𝑎𝑠 𝑎 𝑚𝑢𝑠𝑖𝑐𝑖𝑎𝑛 𝑡𝑜 𝑝𝑙𝑎𝑦? 𝑊𝑒 𝑤𝑎𝑛𝑡 𝑡𝑜 𝑠𝑢𝑝
 𝑝𝑜𝑟𝑡 𝑡ℎ𝑒 𝑚𝑢𝑠𝑖𝑐 𝑎𝑛𝑑 𝑤𝑒 𝑙𝑒𝑡 𝑦𝑜𝑢 𝑖𝑛 𝑓𝑜𝑟 𝑓𝑟𝑒𝑒 𝑎
 𝑛𝑑 𝑔𝑖𝑣𝑒 𝑦𝑜𝑢 𝑡𝑤𝑜 𝑑𝑟𝑖𝑛𝑘 𝑡𝑖𝑐𝑘𝑒𝑡𝑠.\n\n-ac-
LAST-MODIFIED:20190617T132929Z
