BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20221001T140000Z
DTEND:20221002T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20260530T105130Z
UID:1njb46afdt1kjb6vq33l23rag1@google.com
CREATED:20220809T140452Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><b>Tickets at the door:&nbsp\;</b>35EUR (limited ava
 ilability\, come early)<b><br></b></html-blob><br><html-blob><b><br></b></h
 tml-blob><br><html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Welcome to the party!&nbsp\
 ;</b>For this first edition\, we have a fantastic line-up of bands and musi
 cians to carry the music all through the night. Each concert will lead to a
  Jam Session in the style of our regular Jam Cats Session where musicians a
 nd dancers can share the stage. Additionally to that we have planned a lot 
 of cool activities also during the daytime:<br><br><b>Dancers&nbsp\;</b>– T
 his festival is for you! All the parties focus on dance music and to warm y
 ou up we will offer you some fun dance and movement related tasters on Thur
 sday\, Friday and Sunday – as well as some lectures and panel discussions o
 n Friday and Saturday Afternoon. By the way: Come as you are! Feel free to 
 dance solo\, with a partner\, lead\, follow\, switch… Make the music your f
 riend\, bring your own spin to the style\, and don’t be afraid to stand out
 . We make no differentiation based on level\, dance style\, or role and wel
 come all of your happy feet!<br><br><b>Musicians&nbsp\;</b>– We also organi
 ze music workshops during the day where you can practice and learn with pro
 fessional musicians from the Syncopation Society. These workshops will take
  place alongside lectures and panel discussions accessible to all participa
 nts. We will discuss music styles\, history\, and the cultural significance
  of jazz today. More fun awaits you with special daytime activities and tas
 ters curated for the occasion. More to be announced soon.<br><br><b>Everyon
 e&nbsp\;</b>– We want to use this festival as a chance to educate ourselves
  in cultural topics that are connected to\, but go beyond the dance and mus
 ic community today. Which is why we on Friday and Saturday afternoon we off
 er a set of lectures and panel discussions around the topics of Black Ameri
 can Culture\, Diversity and Inclusivity. These topics are very important to
  us\, so we hope you show up and show your support.<br><br><b>Program For S
 aturday:<br><br>16:15 – Panel discussion with Momo: Reflecting the Past and
  the Present…and then?!<br></b>Learning about the history and cultural root
 s of Lindy Hop and Swing is necessary to fully appreciate it. But how can w
 e be sensible and understand the circumstances for black people now and bac
 k then? What could be a good way to discuss the dancing scene and its inclu
 sivity today? Momo created a small portable format that breaks down the pro
 blematic and identifies the inherent racism that European societies have ca
 rried on for centuries. This is a chance to discuss how we can make our sce
 ne more inclusive. And it will be more than just warm words!<u></u><br><u><
 /u><br><u></u><br><u></u><b>20:30 – Talk:&nbsp\;</b><u></u><span><b>Meeting
  Ernie</b></span><br><u></u>Originally from Indianapolis\, Ernie Butler was
  stationed in West Germany during the 1950s where he became basketball coac
 h. In his off-hours he played jazz&nbsp\;and has kept active in the scene e
 ver since. He will talk about his life\, jazz\, dance\, basketball… And pro
 bably a lot more<b><br></b><br><b>21:30 – The Syncopation Society Orchestra
 <br></b>The Syncopation Society Orchestra is the manifestation of our colle
 ctive. Launched by François Perdriau in 2019\, it aims to play a repertoire
  rooted in the early jazz era with a large ensemble. It was made possible b
 y the remarkable work of world-renowned arranger Claus Jacobi. The SSO pres
 ents an impressive line-up of passionate musicians who strive to interpret 
 and even transcend this fantastic music with passion and untameable energy.
 &nbsp\;<br><br><b>23:00 – Late Night Session with the Toolbox Orchestra<br>
 </b>The Toolbox Orchestra is an exotic one-in-a-million-band\, even for the
 ir notorious adopted hometown Berlin: They are an all-female band and origi
 nally started out on self-made instruments straight out of the workshop lik
 e singing saw and washtub bass. Completed by banjo\, guitar\, trumpet and c
 larinet they weave an earthy and unique sound very close to the roots of th
 e music they chose as their playground: the music of the 20’s and early 30’
 s.&nbsp\;<br><br><b>More infos here:</b><br><a href="https://syncopation.de
 /areyou/"><u>https://syncopation.de/areyou/</u></a><br><u></u><br>-of-<br><
 u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220929T132637Z
LOCATION:Ballhaus Prinzenallee\, Prinzenallee 33\, 13359 Berlin\, Germany
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Are You Syncopated?! - The Syncopation Society Orchestra @ Ballhaus
  Prinzenallee
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
