CREATED:20190409T103815Z
DESCRIPTION:Next Friday is Fête de la Musique. The motto of this special da
 y is live music\, for free\, all day long. Although we are not a part of th
 e official program we would like to carry on the spirit and create our own 
 little party - the Fête du Swing!\n\nWe start the social dance already at 2
 0:30 and are going to have live music for you all night long with several b
 ands from Berlin: Open Swing Orchestra Berlin\, Blueberry Bandits\, Marmala
 de Swing\, a yet to be named surprise band and as the grand finale a very s
 pecial jam session!\n\nDonations at the door: 0-10€\nWe want to honor the s
 pirit of the Fête de la Musique\, so all cover fees are donation based\, bu
 t we would love to give all the musicians back some more than just the appl
 ause\, so we appreciate any donations - they will go directly to the musici
 ans :)\n\nps. There will be no regular practice time during that day\, but 
 a mighty lot of social dancing\n\n-ac-
LAST-MODIFIED:20190610T144446Z
LOCATION:SwingStep Berlin - Wedding Prinzenallee 33\, 13359 Berlin\, Deutsc
 hland
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Fête du Swing @ SwingStep Berlin
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20220903T143000Z
DTEND:20220903T160000Z
DTSTAMP:20260530T105130Z
UID:4mag6iriv4ltug82hfjp2f84k5@google.com
CREATED:20220901T113539Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob>Satursday\, 3.9. 16.30 - 18.00<br>Panke Parcours (De
 lphin Stage)<br>Familienzentrum Panke-Haus Soldiner Str. 76\, 13359 Berlin<
 br><br>The Infinite Chocolate Jar plays music for dancing or listening to..
 . well you can try\, not to dance to it. Comprising a mix of identities\, n
 ationalities\, ethnicities and backgrounds\, the band members all present t
 heir unique experiences and personalities while uniting them with their lov
 e for Black American culture and music. Diversity is at their core\, with t
 he goal to create music and spaces which welcome and celebrate all people\,
  as well as working towards creating the same environment within the band a
 nd with the musicians they collaborate with. Stylistically\, the sound is s
 omewhat rooted in and inspired by the swinging blues and jazz music of the 
 ‘20s-‘50s. At the same time\, their music lives in the moment and reflects 
 some of their modern influences and ideas. Like an infinite jar of chocolat
 es\, each sound will come as a delicious surprise :)<br><br>Alea Gardiner (
 Saxophone)<br>Joris Focquaert (Trombone)<br>Fotis-Julius Megas (Double Bass
 )<br>Oliver Fuhrmann (Piano)<br><br>This is our first official gig! Come by
  and dance :D<br><br>-of-</html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220901T113605Z
LOCATION:Familienzentrum Panke-Haus\, Soldiner Str. 76\, 13359 Berlin\, Ger
 many
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The Infinite Chocolate Jar @ Panke Parcours (Delphin Stage)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
