UID:22e5t4sqk9p80e29k5e19gigrs@google.com
CREATED:20220809T140012Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><br><b>Tickets at the door: </b>35EUR (limited avail
 ability\, come early)<br></html-blob><br><html-blob><b><br></b></html-blob>
 <br><html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><b>Welcome to the party!&nbsp\;</b>For 
 this first edition\, we have a fantastic line-up of bands and musicians to 
 carry the music all through the night. Each concert will lead to a Jam Sess
 ion in the style of our regular Jam Cats Session where musicians and dancer
 s can share the stage. Additionally to that we have planned a lot of cool a
 ctivities also during the daytime:<br><br><b>Dancers&nbsp\;</b>– This festi
 val is for you! All the parties focus on dance music and to warm you up we 
 will offer you some fun dance and movement related tasters on Thursday\, Fr
 iday and Sunday – as well as some lectures and panel discussions on Friday 
 and Saturday Afternoon. By the way: Come as you are! Feel free to dance sol
 o\, with a partner\, lead\, follow\, switch… Make the music your friend\, b
 ring your own spin to the style\, and don’t be afraid to stand out. We make
  no differentiation based on level\, dance style\, or role and welcome all 
 of your happy feet!<br><br><b>Musicians&nbsp\;</b>– We also organize music 
 workshops during the day where you can practice and learn with professional
  musicians from the Syncopation Society. These workshops will take place al
 ongside lectures and panel discussions accessible to all participants. We w
 ill discuss music styles\, history\, and the cultural significance of jazz 
 today. More fun awaits you with special daytime activities and tasters cura
 ted for the occasion. More to be announced soon.<br><br><b>Everyone&nbsp\;<
 /b>– We want to use this festival as a chance to educate ourselves in cultu
 ral topics that are connected to\, but go beyond the dance and music commun
 ity today. Which is why we on Friday and Saturday afternoon we offer a set 
 of lectures and panel discussions around the topics of Black American Cultu
 re\, Diversity and Inclusivity. These topics are very important to us\, so 
 we hope you show up and show your support.<br><br><b>Program For Friday:</b
 ><b><br><br>16:15 - Lecture with Joren: The genesis of African and American
  musical traditions with Joren</b><br>Centuries ago\, millions of African p
 eople were being taken away from their lands and drafted into forced labor 
 in the Americas under European rule. This had a profound impact on both con
 tinents\, and certainly also on their musical traditions. Imagine you could
  watch and listen to an interactive radio show\, live\, and the presenter i
 s right there in front of you\, playing good old music\, talking about its 
 context. The goal here is to question How African and American musical trad
 itions have continuously been influencing and inspiring one another since t
 he first day up until present times.<br><br><b>20:30 – Dance taster: Switch
  it! with Momo and Jean</b><br>You are leading and following and you always
  do the same two moves to switch with your partner between the roles? Or ar
 e you used to dance only one role\, but you are also interested in the othe
 r part? We invite you to join and have more fun with exploring to dance bot
 h roles and to learn some more fancy possibilities to switch!<br><br><b>21:
 30 – Meschiya Lake &amp\; The New Movement</b><br>Meschiya Lake has a stron
 g connection to Berlin and a long history. She took a bigger step with her 
 last album “Looking The World Over” recorded and produced in Berlin back in
  2018\, shortly before the pandemic. Now she’s returning to the stage with 
 the New Movement to pick up the story where she left it\, and we will all b
 e there to catch it!<br><br><b>23:00 – Late Night Session with the Careless
  Cats.<br></b>Carried by the powerful personality of Nina Thaler\, the Care
 less Cats is a versatile sextet with a distinctive instrumentation. With a 
 tuba\, a full drum kit and an electric guitar\, they can pull off a totally
  swing sound but also bluesy or slightly Latin if they feel like it\, allow
 ing their front line to shine on cornet and reeds. They present intricate o
 riginal arrangements of famous jazz songs from the 20s to 50s and they will
  host the jam.&nbsp\;<u></u><br><u></u><br><u></u><br><u></u><b>More infos 
 here:</b><br><a href="https://syncopation.de/areyou/">https://syncopation.d
 e/areyou/</a><br><br>-of-<u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220929T132626Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Are You Syncopated?!  - Meschiya Lake & The New Movement @ Ballhaus
  Prinzenallee
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
