DESCRIPTION:Sunday stomps at HBC Berlin! HBC is a huge place\, encompassing
  a bar\, restaurant\, and cinema\, among other things. There you can also f
 ind art exhibitions\, film screenings\, and the occasional rock n' roll mar
 ket (???). \n\nWith 120m2 of beautiful parquet and a great sound system (an
 d no neighbors...)\, the location is perfect for a big dance. We have plent
 y of room for all jazz lovers\; balboa dancers are just as welcome as lindy
  hoppers\, for example. Let's tear it up!\n\nDancing starts at 800PM\, and 
 continues until they kick us out\, probably around 3AM or so.\n\nWith LIVE 
 music. Kind of Dukish\, Berlin's newest big band\, rocks us for the first t
 ime in 2012! The whole group- nine musicians\, including a pianist- playing
  only the best Ellington tunes for our pleasure. Well worth the trip!\n\nEi
 ntritt: 5-10€\, pay what you can afford (support live music! 7€ would be a 
 nice compromise!)- still incredibly cheap for a big band.\n\n-mh
LAST-MODIFIED:20230126T094520Z
LOCATION:.HBC Berlin\, Karl-Liebknecht Str 9
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:LIVE: Kind of Dukish@Sunday Hot Stomp
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
