CREATED:20131024T112904Z
DESCRIPTION:BOOK the whole party pass for only 30€ at http://www.cirque-du-
 solo.com/party-pass/!\n\nAll three parties will take place at the breath-ta
 king former silent theatre Delphi.\n\nFRIDAY 15th November - THE CIRCUS\nDr
 ess code: Circus\nTime: 21.00 - 03.00\nEntry fee: 5€\nHighlight: DJ BATTLE\
 n\nWhat to expect:\nWelcome to the Circus! This is the place where everyone
 s talents are welcome for display\, whether it is a dance\, acrobatic\, sta
 nd-up comedy\, or simply looking amazingly funny. We want to see red noses\
 , hand-stands\, lots of chaos\, and colors! Flying carpets and bearded ladi
 es!\n\nThe Circus is going to rock (uhm... swing) your world with our visit
 ing and local DJs that will be battling for fame and glory! Our MC and DJ c
 oordinator Shorty George will host this battle between the following line-u
 p:\nDJ Kris (Ghentlemen)\, Belgium\nDJ Greta\, Germany\nDJ Chris “The Wild 
 Man” Wild\, Germany\nDJ Fröken Frida\, Sweden\n\n\nSATURDAY 16th November -
  THE BALL\nDress code: Fancy. Evening dress to kill and tuxedo/suit to make
  the ladies go OMG!\nTime: 21.00 - 04.00\nEntry fee: 15€\nHighlight: Nomad 
 Swing live music from Belgium\n\nWhat to expect:\nA night at the Delphi jus
 t as if we were back in the 1920s\, when this was Berlin's cultural hotspot
 . Stars like Marlene Dietrich and Fritz Lang were there. The Delphi theater
  miraculously survived WWII and remained closed during GDR times. In fact\,
  the theater has remained closed to the general public since the war and is
  still today.\nCome dressed like a star and experience the glamour and flai
 r of this extraordinary venue. \nOur feet will be swinging to music from No
 mad Swing\, a group of very talented musicians from Flanders who have a pas
 sion for music from the twenties to the fifties and already stunned many cr
 owds of dancing and non-dancing audience.\n\n\nSUNDAY 17th November - THE C
 ABARET\nDress code: Come as you are\nTime: 20.00 - 03.00\nBuffet: 20.00 - 2
 1.00 (buffet reservation will be available soon)\nEntry fee: 15€ \nHighligh
 t: The Cabaret show (starts at 21.00)\n\nWhat to expect:\nYou are sitting i
 n your chair\, playing with your fork\, and can't wait until the curtains f
 inally fall – for the greatest cabaret show on earth. You only heard rumors
  about the (in)famous acts waiting in the wings to present you their finest
  numbers. Be ready for Dancing\, Acrobatics\, Juggling\, Clownerie\, Magic\
 , and ... Dancing! \n\nBe glad you ordered the Gala-Buffet in advance\, so 
 at least you have something to chew on to calm down your nerves...\n\nAfter
 -show party with our amazing DJs.\n\nAll information also on website:\nhttp
 ://www.cirque-du-solo.com/parties/\n\nand Facebook:\nhttps://www.facebook.c
 om/events/585540338148951/?fref=ts\n\nThese parties are part of Cirque du S
 olo 2013 which also offers Authentic Jazz workshops:\nhttp://www.cirque-du-
 solo.com/workshop\n\n- OF -
LAST-MODIFIED:20230126T095339Z
LOCATION:Ehemaliges Stummfilmkino Delphi Berlin - Gustav-Adolf-Straße 2\, 1
 3086 Berlin\, Germany
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Cirque du Solo - THE CIRCUS
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
