 p>    <p dir="ltr"><span>WORKSHOP PRESENTATIONS</span></p>    <p dir="ltr">
 <span>SOCIAL DANCE WITH DJs LIZA LARK + MISS TILLIE</span></p>    <br>    <
 p dir="ltr"><span>18h30 doors</span></p>    <p dir="ltr"><span>19h program 
 - starts sharp !</span></p>    <p dir="ltr"><span>21h social dance</span></
 p>    <br>    <p dir="ltr"><span>Donations at the door. </span></p>    <p d
 ir="ltr"><span>Hosted by Bellmer Balboa</span></p>    <br>    <p dir="ltr">
 <span>This special night highlights the presence and power of female musici
 ans on stage. </span></p>    <p dir="ltr"><span>A night to celebrate all sy
 ncopated sisters and to break the narrative that there are “hardly any fema
 le musicians in the scene” or that “they are not good enough”.</span></p>  
   <p dir="ltr"><span>After three days of getting together during this first
  edition of the Syncopated Sisters residency\, playing music\, exchanging e
 xperiences as well as working on future visions\, this night will show and 
